  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "2a1a56fd-2fe3-43f2-a8e1-aa43bb5d8fca",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        320,
        -272
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 764,
        "height": 1240,
        "content": "# Migrate SmartSuite comments into Monday.com\n\nCopy the comment history from every SmartSuite record into a long-text column on the matching Monday.com item. Useful as a one-off migration when moving a team from SmartSuite to Monday, so the discussion history moves across with the data instead of being lost.\n\n### How it works\n1. A manual trigger starts the run and a Set node holds all API keys and IDs in one place.\n2. Records are pulled from a SmartSuite table in pages, then processed five at a time so neither API is overloaded.\n3. For each record, its comments are fetched. Records with no comments are skipped straight away.\n4. Comments are flattened into a dated plain-text archive, with mentions preserved, each comment trimmed to 150 characters and the whole block capped at 1900 characters to fit a Monday long-text column.\n5. The matching Monday item is found by searching a text column for the SmartSuite record ID, and the archive is written to the comments column. A short delay keeps the run inside API rate limits.\n\n### Setup\n1. Open Set config variables and fill in every placeholder: your SmartSuite API key, workspace ID and table ID, your Monday API key and board ID.\n2. Add the two Monday column IDs: the text column holding the SmartSuite record ID, and the long-text column that will receive the comments.\n3. Run once with a small batch limit to confirm the mapping, then raise it.\n\n### Customization\n- Change batch_limit and current_offset to migrate in pages through a large table.\n- Edit the character limits in Format comments into text if your column allows more."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
